# Files that must never be part of a published app.
#
# .gitignore keeps files out of git. It does not keep them out of what Replit
# publishes: a published app is built from the files on disk. This file does.
# Only the web app is published; everything below is either private or not part of it.

# Private material that can be present in a workspace: the puller's output under
# every name it uses, link lists, and browser profiles (a profile holds a sign-in).
/sessions*/
/puller/sessions*/
/session_*
/raw/
/all_sessions.md
/*links*.txt
/*profile*/
/*user-data*/
/CLAUDE.local.md
/.claude/
/.config/
/.local/
/.cache/
/.pythonlibs/
/.upm/

# Other components of this repository
/apple/
/puller/
/reference/

# The web app's documents, test fixtures and reference code
/web/docs/
/web/fixtures/
/web/reference/
